  ✕ Invalid conversion
   ╭─[test.lis:4:3]
 3 │   let b: byte = 65;
 4 │   b as string
   ·   ─────┬─────
   ·        ╰── cannot convert `byte` to `string`
 5 │ }
   ╰────
  help: Use `[b] as string` to preserve the byte (may be invalid UTF-8), or convert through a rune to encode as a codepoint: `let r = b as rune; r as string`. A byte has two readings as a string · code: [infer.invalid_conversion]
